From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: SHShellFolderView_Message, SignalFileOpen, SHWaitForFileToOpen (3707)

shell32: SHShellFolderView_Message, SignalFileOpen, SHWaitForFileToOpen

SHShellFolderView_Message finds the folder view in the window it is given (the
view window itself or the window around it) and carries out the SFVM_ request
in it: REARRANGE, ADDOBJECT, REMOVEOBJECT, UPDATEOBJECT, GETSELECTEDOBJECTS,
SETITEMPOS, SETCLIPBOARD and SETPOINTS, returning what each is documented to.
SHWaitForFileToOpen (SHWFF_ADD, SHWFF_WAIT, SHWFF_REMOVE) and SignalFileOpen
now work across processes through a named event per file.
---
